# The build context is sent to the daemon in full, so anything large or
# sensitive that is not needed to compile must be excluded here.
#
# `corpus/` above all: it is the local evidence corpus, tens of gigabytes of
# real device images, and it is git-ignored precisely so it never leaves this
# machine. A build context that swept it up would copy it into the daemon and
# potentially into an image layer.
corpus/
tests/corpus/local/

build/
vcpkg_installed/
out/
.git/
.github/
.cache/
*.o
*.a
compile_commands.json

# docs/ and scripts/ stay: `ctest` runs scripts/check_docs.py, which reads
# both, so excluding them would turn the docs gate into a silent skip.
